t the chosen tier per key, and names a key by its one label or, with several labels, by the key itself. Tier choice, decks totals and sorting are unchanged. The new `splitOptions` returns `main` (share \u2265 `MAIN_SHARE`) and `other` (everything else, including null share), order kept.\n- **`web/src/components/rcq/InputsCard.tsx`**: a `showOther` state (default false). Chips are main, then the other options that are shown or picked, then the missing picked keys. An `Other (N)` / `Fewer` button sits after the chips, styled like them, with `aria-expanded`.\n- **`web/src/views/RcqView.tsx`**: the reset-based window and `useMetagameStatus` are gone. The chips read `{ days: CHIP_WINDOW_DAYS }` with `CHIP_WINDOW_DAYS = 14`, and the share note is the sentence from the spec.\n\n**Choices I made where the spec was silent**\n\n- The \"Other (N)\" button appears when some other options are unpicked, or while expanded. Once every other option is picked and the list is collapsed, there is nothing hidden, so no button appears.\n- The \"Other\" button is rendered even when there are no main chips, so a collapsed list with only hidden options still has a way to open.\n\n**Checks**\n\n- `pnpm --dir web test`: 23 files, 527 tests passed. This includes the new `splitOptions` and per-key sum tests in `rcq.test.ts`, which I did not edit.\n- `pnpm --dir web exec tsc -b`: exit 0.\n- `pnpm --dir web lint`: oxlint printed no problems. I read the output rather than capturing its exit code.\n\nI did not run the app or check the rendered page in a browser, so the layout of the new button is unverified visually.", "ttft_ms": 1630, "type": "result", "duration_ms": 49004, "uuid": "ea68f0fd-8a83-487b-b49e-fefdcc0da2f9", "ttft_stream_ms": 1545, "time_to_request_ms": 540, "first_content_frame_ms": 1545, "queued_turn_count": 0, "result_index": 0}
